// golden_test.go — T-43: the generated-golden differential for the
// handdelivery module's T-43 surface — the walled picker, the batch
// consume, the queue stamp, the fifth door's to-do list, and the
// hand_fetch_result shape.
//
// testdata/handdelivery.golden.json is generated by
// testdiff/goldens/dump_handdelivery.py from the unmodified reference
// (assadigit/GitCurator @ 98f4fc7, the pinned venv's CPython 3.12.15
// stdlib) with hand_delivery's clock frozen at 2026-10-17 12:00 — no
// per-run facts inside. The reference module is core/ and stdlib-only
// (no GUI-layer stubs needed); the auto-door page in the consume flow
// is a REAL page, so the reference's own page_is_real verdict and the
// port's honest degrade (PageIsRealFn unset until T-44) agree. The
// T-40 sections (enqueue / README / take / redo / heal) stay pinned
// by internal/websitepipeline's golden — extend, never duplicate.
//
// THE LAW: goldens are never hand-edited; a divergence is either a Go
// bug (fix the port) or a reference behavior change (regenerate + say
// so in the commit).
package handdelivery

